    {
      "text": "####What Type of RDD Does Your Transformation Return?\n- loosing type information when converted to Dataframe\n- type Row is not strongly type..it can be Any hence running operation on the same won't compile\n- One of the advantages of the Dataset API is that it is strongly typed, so the\nvalues in each row will retain their type information even after conversion to an RDD.",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "9cdd00a3797544299c848"
    },
    {
